# Duvet generated artifacts. Both are re-derived from the specs on every
# `duvet report`, so committing them would duplicate the spec text and let it
# drift. The snapshot at .duvet/snapshot.txt IS committed — it is what
# `duvet report --ci` verifies against.
.duvet/reports/
.duvet/requirements/

# Python bytecode and build output.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments. The workspace uses a single .venv at the root, created
# by `uv sync`; per-member environments are never correct here because the
# members share one resolution.
.venv/
venv/

# The upstream clone `just vendored-drift` compares against. A scratch copy of
# somebody else's repository, re-fetched on every run.
.upstream-drift/

# Model weights. Fetched and hash-verified by `just models` from the pinned
# sources in services/groundstation/src/reachy_groundstation/models/registry.py,
# and never committed: the registry records where each one came from and what it
# must hash to, which is what a licence audit reads instead of the bytes.
.models/

# Tool caches.
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Coverage output. Diff-scoped gating regenerates these on every run.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Untracked local files that carry environment-specific values. Each one has a
# tracked `.example` sibling documenting its shape — the examples arrive with
# the changes that introduce the files (0002 for the environment files, 0010 for
# the Ansible inventory). Real hostnames, addresses and credentials live only in
# these ignored copies.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
provisioning/ansible/inventory.ini

# The idempotency gate's scratch directory: an ephemeral SSH key pair, a
# generated inventory, a fixture wheel and the declaration applied to the
# container target. Every one of them is made by `just provision-target-up` and
# thrown away by `just provision-target-down`; none of them is ever committed.
.provisioning-target/

# Ansible's own caches and retry files, written beside the playbook.
provisioning/ansible/*.retry
.ansible/
